xnu 0504: play one pcm period through the adsp

Port the rest of the zizhan AudioReach builders (BSD-2-Clause-Patent,
ShengAudioReach.c) into mondrian_audioreach.c and its header: the
playback stream graph (shared-memory endpoint, decoder and converter,
linked to the device graph's I2S instance), the PCM output and
shared-memory media formats, the native memory map and the buffer
write. The worker then opens and configures both graphs, allocates
16 KiB of physically contiguous memory, maps it with the donor's
address form (physical | bit 32), prepares and starts the device graph
and the stream, and sends one 10 ms period (480 frames of 32-bit
stereo). It logs the map handle and the write-done address and status,
stops and closes both graphs and unmaps the buffer.

Measured 2026-11-27: both graphs and all three formats answer status 0,
but the allocation lands above 4 GiB (pa=0x84a200000), where the map's
upper word is no longer 1, so the map answers status 1 and the write
does not run. This unit has no free DRAM page below 4 GiB; the donor
reaches a high buffer through the apps-SMMU SID 0x1801, which this
port does not program yet. The AW88261 amplifiers are not programmed
either, so nothing is audible.
